Z||000001||Raydar||10-06-2000||09:43 AM||||Probably not. They look like a RWD offset. <BR>Probably a Camaro / S-10 / Monte Carlo bolt pattern, which is different from a Fiero bolt pattern. <BR>They do look cool, though. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR>88 Formula T-Top <BR>88 Coupe (soon to receive transplant.)<BR>88 "pretzeled" Formula <P>Out of my mind.<BR>Back in five minutes.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Tigger||10-06-2000||09:53 AM||||Yep, they look cool but they need to be a 5 bolt pattern on 100mm to even bolt up.  Even if they did bolt up the wheels would extend out from fenderwells and well, people would start thinking ricer.<P>Check out <A HREF="http://www.discounttire.com" TARGET=_blank>www.Discounttire.com</A> or <A HREF="http://www.tirerack.com" TARGET=_blank>www.Tirerack.com</A><P>You might find some similar wheels in these sites and I think you can try them out on a picture of a Fiero in the site.<P>------------------<BR>T-T-F-N, Tah Tah For Now!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tigger.gif">          <BR> <A HREF="mailto:RacingStripes@hotmail.com">RacingStripes@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||1
